+# Homepage performance monitoring
+
+`performance-monitor.js` loads deferred and observes browser-attributed contentful
+updates, including asynchronous paints after an interaction. Stable
+`data-performance-source` labels identify navbar controls, Order Now, and each
+Seasonal Favorites card (including its View Details link). It does not change
+link behavior or create client-side routes.
+
+Read `window.dailyGrindPerformance.support` for API availability and
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()` for the latest 200 reports. Subscribe
+before interactions to stream reports to an existing analytics integration:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Pass detail to your analytics client here.
+});
+```
+
+No data is sent over the network by this monitor. Reports contain numeric timing
+data and fixed control labels, not DOM elements, text, or URL query strings.
+
+- `interaction-contentful-paint`: `duration` is milliseconds from interaction start
+  to presentation on screen, not a page-relative timestamp. The browser may emit
+  multiple progressively larger paints for one interaction; group by
+  `timeOrigin` and `interactionId`. `source` is null when attribution is unavailable
+  or the interaction is outside the labeled controls. Buffered inputs predating
+  monitor installation may lack a source label.
+- `soft-navigation`: `fcpDuration` and `lcpDuration` measure from the initiating
+  interaction. The monitor seeds LCP with the browser's largest paint, then matches
+  subsequent paints by `interactionId`, including paints made before a URL update.
+  Reports finalize at the next soft navigation, when the document is hidden, or
+  on `pagehide`. Lifecycle flushing drains queued observer records first.
+
+Both APIs are progressive enhancements. Unsupported entry types are skipped;
+there is no synthetic paint estimate. These are contentful-update metrics, not
+INP or initial-document LCP. The current site's links perform full document
+navigations, so they do not produce soft-navigation reports or measure the
+destination document's paint. Soft-navigation reports become available if
+client-side routing is added and the browser detects a qualifying transition.
+Clicks without a new contentful paint produce no paint report.
+
+Run the non-browser checks with `node --test performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
+They exercise a mocked PerformanceObserver, not browser rendering or API support.
+API reference: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/soft-navigations
